+	// device_scheduler::time() reports the cached m_callback_timer_expire_time
+	// while a timer callback is running, and only m_basetime is part of the save
+	// buffer. If the state is loaded from inside a callback (a Lua/plugin frame
+	// notifier, or netplay's frame gate), that cache still holds the pre-load
+	// timeline's instant after m_basetime has been rewound, so time() reports a
+	// stale "now" and the first timeslice runs off the restored timeline — the
+	// reloaded machine diverges from the one that never stopped (T46). Re-base the
+	// cache on the restored m_basetime; when no callback is active this is a no-op.
+	if (m_callback_timer != nullptr)
+		m_callback_timer_expire_time = m_basetime;
+
